    "faq": {
      "type": "bella-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does virtual room design work?",
            "answer": "You share photos of the room, measurements if you have them, and your style preferences online. A designer builds the room digitally, furnishes it, renders it as a photorealistic image and refines it with your feedback, so you can preview the finished space before you buy, paint or move anything. With Bella's Design My Room, every photo you send comes back as three designs in different furniture styles, made by a real interior designer."
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I take a picture of my room and redesign it?",
            "answer": "Yes, that's exactly how Design My Room works. Take a clear, wide photo of the room, empty or furnished, upload it after checkout, and a Bella designer redesigns it three ways. You see new furniture, decor and layout in your own space, not in a generic showroom."
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I hire someone to design my room online?",
            "answer": "Yes. With Design My Room you hire a professional interior designer online for one room or multiple rooms, with no site visit, no travel fees and no hourly billing. Order one photo per room, send your photos and style, and your designs arrive in 24–48 hours. We work with clients across the United States and Canada."
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much does it cost to design a room virtually?",
            "answer": "Design My Room is one flat price per photo, shown at the top of this page, and every photo includes three designs. There are no hourly fees and no subscription. For comparison, Angi's 2026 cost data puts in-person interior designers at $100 to $500 an hour, with the average project costing $8,550."
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does virtual room design take?",
            "answer": "24 to 48 hours from the time you upload your photos. After delivery you have two weeks of unlimited free revisions, and if a design still isn't right, we rework it or refund it."
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does my room need to be empty?",
            "answer": "No. Design My Room works from photos of empty or furnished rooms. Send the room as it is today, and your designer works from the space, walls, windows and dimensions in the photo."
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I choose the styles for my designs?",
            "answer": "Browse our <a href=\"/pages/lookbook\">Look Book</a> and send the codes of the sets you like with your photos, name a style, or leave the choice to your designer. Look Book styles include Contemporary, Modern Farmhouse, Scandinavian, Coastal, Mid-Century Modern, Traditional and Transitional."
          }
        },
        "q8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you design a living room, bedroom or dining room?",
            "answer": "Yes. Design My Room is built for the residential rooms you furnish, such as a living room, bedroom, dining room or home office, and the Look Book has designer sets for each. If the problem is dated floors, cabinets or fixtures rather than furniture, <a href=\"/products/virtual-renovation-service\">virtual renovation</a> is the better fit."
          }
        },
        "q9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is Design My Room an online interior design service?",
            "answer": "Yes. It's a virtual interior design service with one clear deliverable: photorealistic designs of your own room that you can compare side by side. Many online design services deliver mood boards, floor plans or 3D renderings; Design My Room shows you the finished room. For a full comparison of online and in-person options, read our <a href=\"/pages/interior-design-consultation\">online interior design consultation</a> guide."
          }
        },
        "q10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does Design My Room include a floor plan?",
            "answer": "No. Design My Room is a design and visualization service: you get three photorealistic designs of your room. It doesn't include a measured floor plan, a site visit, furniture purchasing or construction. If you need a layout drawing, <a href=\"/products/2d-3d-floor-plan-service\">2D and 3D floor plans</a> are a separate service."
          }
        },
        "q11": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's the difference between Design My Room and virtual staging?",
            "answer": "Both are done by Bella's interior designers, but they solve different problems. Virtual staging furnishes listing photos for a home that's for sale: one MLS-ready design per photo. Design My Room gives you three designs per photo, so you can compare styles and choose a direction for your own space. Selling a home? Start with <a href=\"/products/virtual-staging\">virtual staging</a>."
          }
        },
        "q12": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can AI or ChatGPT redesign my room?",
            "answer": "AI tools, including image features in chatbots like ChatGPT, can generate a redesigned room from a photo in seconds, and they're a fun source of ideas. The trade-off is accuracy: they often change windows, walls or proportions, and getting one specific detail right can take many tries. Every Design My Room design is composed by hand by a real interior designer, never AI, so the room stays your room."
          }
        },
        "q13": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I design my room online for free?",
            "answer": "Yes, if you do the work yourself. Room design apps such as Planner 5D, Homestyler and Roomstyler have free plans: you draw or scan a floor plan, then drag and drop furniture on your phone, web browser or desktop and preview the room in 3D. In Apartment Therapy's 2025 review, the free plans were useful but limited, with many items behind a paywall. Design My Room is the done-for-you option: a professional designer creates the designs and delivers photorealistic images of your actual room."
          }
        },
        "q14": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use the designs in a property listing?",
            "answer": "Yes, with disclosure. If a design appears in a listing or in marketing, label it as virtually staged and keep the original photo available. For listing photos, <a href=\"/products/virtual-staging\">virtual staging</a> is built for the MLS."
          }
        },
        "q15": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if I don't like the designs?",
            "answer": "Ask for changes. You can request adjustments to the layout, colors or furniture in any of your three designs, and revisions are unlimited and free for two weeks after delivery. If a design still isn't right after rework, we refund that photo."
          }
        },
        "q16": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What software do your designers use?",
            "answer": "Professional 3D modeling and rendering tools, including 3ds Max and the Corona renderer, which simulates how light falls on furniture and materials, with every image finished by hand in Photoshop. We don't use AI generators or template rooms."
          }
        }
      },
